<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Giessen</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gießen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Giessen is a university town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahn">Lahn</a> river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. It was the main town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-hesse">Upper Hesse</a>, a province of the landgraviate and later grand duchy of Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a>, whose ruler founded its university in 1607. The chemist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justus-von-liebig">Justus von Liebig</a> taught there from 1824 to 1852, making it a leading centre of chemistry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/giessen.jpg" alt="Giessen" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ralf Lotys (Sicherlich) · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2004-JLU_Gie%C3%9Fen_Sicherlich.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
